      "status": "passed",
      "summary": "Selected a diversity-compliant small battery-awareness and charge-qualification supervisor with a closed 6/14/12/5 specification and one principal decision owner.",
      "questions_for_model": [
        "Can the trusted SysML-AADL/GUMBO subset realize the Charge Qualification Owner's two finite local state variables, initialization, pre-state guards, and all twelve same-evaluation post-state/output cases without duplicating the decision?",
        "What behavior-free containment and boundary-delegation structure is required to realize the fourteen semantic interactions at depth 1..2, and what raw connection count results while preserving the semantic inventory?",
        "Can local contracts express the joint charger/flight-context classification and the two separate decision-plus-battery output derivations without an unsupported construct or competing policy owner?"
      ],
      "repair_actions": [],
      "diversity": {
        "selected_primary_scope": "battery-awareness and charging qualification",
        "closest_baseline": "replicate-1 lifecycle transition governor owning or deriving Off/Standby/Charging/Ready/Flying",
        "primary_scope_differs": true,
        "controlled_purpose_differs": true,
        "differing_dimensions": [
          "boundary",
          "state_ownership",
          "interaction_topology",
          "priority_policy"
        ],
        "why_not_extension_or_rename": "The selected owner stores only charge authorization and recovery state, consumes charge-specific battery/charger/flight-context/intent evidence, and emits charge authorization plus battery evidence; no state, case, or output can select or reconstruct a lifecycle phase. Integrating it with the baseline would require a new cross-boundary allocation for consuming its evidence, so it is a separate supervisory purpose rather than a renamed or repartitioned lifecycle state machine."
